          </svg>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p class="dynamics-boundary">{t(`这段曲线是训练过程证据，不是 128 题最终终评。${dynamics3B.acceptedRolloutsTotal.toLocaleString('en-US')} 次正式环境尝试里，ledger 记录的 engineering invalid、parser repair、invalid-action termination 都是 0。它支持排除“训练根本没工作”这个简单解释；下一问变成：这些学习为什么只有限地转化成最终任务能力？`, `These are training-process measurements, not the frozen 128-task final evaluation. Across ${dynamics3B.acceptedRolloutsTotal.toLocaleString('en-US')} formal environment attempts, the ledger records zero engineering-invalid, parser-repair, or invalid-action-termination events. That rules out the simple claim that training never worked; the next question is why the learning translates only partially into final task ability.`)}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('曲线口径、ledger 来源与 checkpoint 回放边界', 'Curve semantics, ledger provenance, and checkpoint-replay boundary')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">06 / 12</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="horizon-diagnostic" class="briefing-slide tone-gold" aria-labelledby="horizon-title">
    <div class="slide-inner horizon-slide">
      <h2 id="horizon-title">{t('多给 15 步，模型还是在几个导航动作里打转', 'Fifteen extra steps still leave the model looping through the same navigation actions')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('我们先看了真实轨迹，而不只看最后的 0 分：15 步版本里，模型反复执行 next（下一页）和 back（返回），一直没有进入 buy（购买）。所以当时最自然的怀疑是：会不会只是 15 步太短，还没来得及做完？', 'We inspected the actual traces rather than only the zero reward. At 15 steps the model repeatedly used next and back and never reached a buy transition. The natural hypothesis was therefore that 15 steps might simply be too short to finish.')}</p>
      <div class="before-after horizon-compare">
        <div class="before"><span>15 步</span><strong>next ↔ back ↔ next …</strong><p>{t('几个导航动作反复出现；轨迹走满 15 步，仍没有进入购买动作，任务得分为 0。', 'A few navigation actions repeat; the trace reaches the 15-step limit without a buy action, and the task score is zero.')}</p></div>
        <div class="after"><span>30 步</span><strong>{t('多出来的 15 步没有打开新路径', 'The extra 15 steps do not open a new path')}</strong><p>{t('模型仍在同样几个导航动作里打转，没有进入 buy；BASE-15 和 BASE-30 的任务得分都为 0。', 'The model keeps cycling through the same navigation actions and still never reaches buy; both BASE-15 and BASE-30 score zero.')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="horizon-proof" aria-label={t('排除工程和任务不可达解释的补充证据', 'Supporting evidence against simple engineering and reachability explanations')}>
        <span><strong>64 / 64</strong>{t(' 次模型尝试有效', ' model attempts valid')}</span>
        <span><strong>Δ = 0.0</strong>{t(' 每个 30−15 配对都没有改善', ' for every paired 30−15 comparison')}</span>
        <span><strong>6 / 8</strong>{t(' 个任务经 oracle 核对可到达目标', ' tasks had oracle-reachable targets')}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="resolution-box"><strong>{t('于是我们知道：问题不在“差几步就能做完”', 'So the problem is not simply “the model needed a few more steps”')}</strong><p>{t('步数翻倍后，行为模式本身没有改变。至少在可达任务上，瓶颈更像动作选择 / 规划，而不是 horizon。我们因此停止继续加步数，转去检查下一个假设。', 'Doubling the horizon did not change the behavior pattern. On the reachable tasks, the bottleneck looked more like action selection/planning than horizon length. We therefore stopped extending max_steps and moved to the next hypothesis.')}</p></div>
      <p class="slide-number">07 / 12</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="capacity-diagnostic" class="briefing-slide tone-gold" aria-labelledby="capacity-title">
    <div class="slide-inner">
      <h2 id="capacity-title">{t('我们把记忆容量翻倍了', 'We doubled the memory capacity')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('我们先把文本记忆模块一次生成能用的 token 上限从', 'We first increased the Text Memory generation token cap from')} <strong>2048 → 4096</strong>{t('，仍然饱和。最后不再继续堆容量，而是改成有边界的分块处理：同一批 20 条记录修复一次后若仍饱和，才固定拆成 10 + 10，分别压缩再合并。', '. It still saturated. Instead of continuing to add capacity, we switched to bounded decomposition: if the same 20 records still saturate after one repair pass, split them deterministically into 10 + 10, compress each half, then merge them.')}</p>
      <div class="before-after">
        <div class="before"><span>{t('单次容量实验', 'single-call capacity')}</span><strong>2048 → 4096</strong><p>{t('单纯把 token 上限翻倍仍然没有解决容量失败。', 'Doubling the token cap alone did not resolve the capacity failure.')}</p></div>
        <div class="after"><span>{t('结构化处理', 'structured recovery')}</span><strong>20 {t('条记录', 'records')} → 10 + 10</strong><p>{t('先保留原来的 20 条记录；如果同一批记录修复一次后仍然饱和，才固定拆成前 10 + 后 10，分别压缩后再合并。', 'Keep the original 20 records first; only if the same records still saturate after one repair pass do we split into first 10 + last 10, compress each half, then merge.')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="resolution-box"><strong>{t('最终怎么解决容量饱和', 'How we ultimately handled saturation')}</strong><p>{t('最终采用 A2 方案：先处理全部 20 条原始记录；如果达到容量上限，就用同 20 条、同样顺序再修复一次；如果仍然饱和，才固定拆成前 10 + 后 10，分别压缩后再合并。这样把“容量一满就卡死”变成一个有边界、可复现的恢复路径；但它只解决容量故障，不等于证明最终 WebShop 分数因此提高。', 'We adopted the A2 procedure: process all 20 original records; if the output reaches the capacity limit, repair the same 20 in the same order once; only if it still saturates do we split deterministically into first 10 + last 10, compress each half, and merge them. This turns saturation from a blocking failure into a bounded, reproducible recovery path; it does not by itself prove a higher final WebShop score.')}</p></div>
      <p class="slide-number">08 / 12</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="mechanism" class="briefing-slide tone-gold" aria-labelledby="mechanism-title">
    <div class="slide-inner">
      <h2 id="mechanism-title">{t('TaskVector（参数更新方向）：检验模型连续更新时到底学到了什么', 'TaskVector (parameter-update direction): test what successive updates actually learn')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('如果连续两次更新真的学到了同一种东西，它们在参数空间里应该形成一个可测量的方向。TaskVector 把这个方向写成一个可以主动加回模型、拿掉或反向施加的量。', 'If successive updates learn something coherent, they should form a measurable direction in parameter space. TaskVector turns that direction into an intervention we can add, remove, or reverse.')}</p>
      <div class="mechanism-math">
        <div class="formula-card">
          <strong>{t('定义一个参数方向', 'Define a parameter direction')}</strong>
          <div class="equation">τ = ΔW<sub>R49</sub> − ΔW<sub>R27</sub></div>
          <div class="equation">‖τ‖<sub>F</sub> = 0.608</div>
          <p>{t('然后比较 +τ、−τ 和同范数随机方向，看行为变化是不是“方向特异”的，而不只是因为参数动得更多。', 'Then compare +τ, −τ, and norm-matched random directions to test whether behavior is direction-specific rather than merely responding to larger parameter movement.')}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="formula-card">
          <strong>{t('一次失败反而让定义更严格', 'A failed construction made the definition stricter')}</strong>
          <p>{t('最早的 75% 和 100% 两个锚点都落在第 49 轮保存的同一个参数状态（R49），所以 τ=0。这个结果说明原构造不可识别；我们随后改用第 14、27、49 轮三个真实不同的参数状态。', 'The first 75% and 100% anchors both resolved to the same saved Round-49 parameter state (R49), so τ=0. That made the construction unidentifiable; we rebuilt it from genuinely distinct Round-14, Round-27, and Round-49 states.')}</p>
          <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('完整技术推导与实验门槛', 'Full technical derivation and experimental thresholds')}</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="slide-number">09 / 12</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="gdr" class="briefing-slide tone-rose" aria-labelledby="gdr-title">
    <div class="slide-inner">
      <h2 id="gdr-title">{t('GDR：我们给 SD-LoRA 参数更新加了一道筛选', 'GDR: adding a selective gate to SD-LoRA parameter updates')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('按我们原先的 OpenEVO Stage 2 设计，每次发生参数进化，就会训练一个 SD-LoRA 更新并写入后续模型。1.7B 长周期实验里，实际发生并训练了 44 次这样的更新。后来我们加入 GDR（Gated Delta Rule）：更新先训练，再根据短期效果决定是否真正写入模型。', 'In our original OpenEVO Stage 2 design, each parameter-evolution event trains an SD-LoRA update that enters the next model state. The 1.7B long-horizon run actually produced and trained 44 such updates. We later added GDR (Gated Delta Rule): train the update first, then use its short-term effect to decide whether it is written into the continuing model.')}</p>
      <div class="before-after gdr-flow">
        <div class="before"><span>{t('原本的参数进化', 'Original parameter evolution')}</span><strong>{t('发生进化 → 训练 SD-LoRA → 更新参数', 'evolve → train SD-LoRA → update parameters')}</strong><p>{t('一次参数进化对应一个真正训练出来的 SD-LoRA 更新。1.7B 这条线一共发生了 44 次。', 'Each parameter-evolution event corresponds to one actually trained SD-LoRA update. The 1.7B line produced 44 of them.')}</p></div>
        <div class="after"><span>GDR = Gated Delta Rule</span><strong>{t('发生进化 → 训练 SD-LoRA → 先筛选 → 再决定是否写入', 'evolve → train SD-LoRA → gate it → decide whether to write')}</strong><p>{t('44 个更新都训练了，但 GDR 最后只让 7 个进入后续模型。其余 37 个训练结果被拒绝。', 'All 44 updates were trained, but GDR admitted only 7 into later model states; the other 37 trained updates were rejected.')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="bottom-claim">{t('所以 44 不是人为设定的“更新预算”，而是这条实验里真实发生的 44 次 SD-LoRA 参数进化。看到 44 → 7 之后，我们开始追问：GDR 会不会筛得过于保守？', 'So 44 is not an arbitrary “update budget”; it is the 44 SD-LoRA parameter-evolution events that actually occurred in this run. Seeing 44 → 7 led to the next question: is GDR filtering too conservatively?')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('GDR 的判定逻辑与完整实验定义', 'GDR decision logic and full experimental definition')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">10 / 12</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="directapply" class="briefing-slide tone-green" aria-labelledby="directapply-title">
    <div class="slide-inner">
      <h2 id="directapply-title">{t('DirectApply：拿掉 GDR 的否决权，只改这一个变量', 'DirectApply: remove only the GDR veto')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('两条路线都训练同样的 SD-LoRA 候选；区别只有一个：GDR 可以拒绝候选，DirectApply 对满足共同训练条件的候选直接应用。', 'Both routes train the same kind of SD-LoRA candidate. The single intended difference is whether GDR may veto the update or DirectApply applies a qualifying candidate directly.')}</p>
      <div class="before-after">
        <div class="before"><span>GDR</span><strong>{t('训练 Δ → 再决定要不要更新', 'train Δ → decide whether to update')}</strong><p>{t('候选可能被拒绝，因此后续模型不一定看到这次学习。', 'A candidate can be rejected, so later states may never see that learning event.')}</p></div>
        <div class="after"><span>DirectApply</span><strong>{t('训练 Δ → 直接进入后续模型', 'train Δ → apply it to the next state')}</strong><p>{t('不再用 GDR 做第二次否决。这样才能直接问：44→7 的筛选到底帮助了长期学习，还是限制了它？', 'There is no second GDR veto. This directly tests whether the 44→7 filtering helped long-term learning or constrained it.')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="plain-language-result"><strong>{t('当前状态', 'Current state')}</strong><p>{t('DirectApply 的独立实验已经启动，但最终冻结分数还没有收口，所以结果表保持空白。由于暑期考核时间点就在这里，我们目前的能力天花板故事先讲到这里。', 'The independent DirectApply experiment has started, but its frozen final score is not sealed yet, so the results table remains blank. At the summer-review cutoff, this is where the current ceiling story stops.')}</p></div>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('严谨性、重复性与复现实验细节', 'Rigor, reproducibility, and execution details')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">11 / 12</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="next" class="briefing-slide briefing-final" aria-labelledby="next-title">
    <div class="slide-inner">
      <h2 id="next-title">{t('下一步优先级：先做机制，还是先做 SEED 匹配比较？', 'Next priority: mechanism first, or matched SEED comparison first?')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('现在已经有一条清楚的研究链：7B 给出第一条长周期基线；1.7B / 3B 帮我们快速排除错误解释；TaskVector 和 44→7 又把问题推进到参数机制与更新准入。下一步两条线都值得做，但优先级不同。', 'We now have a coherent chain: 7B provides the long-horizon baseline; 1.7B / 3B let us falsify explanations quickly; TaskVector and the 44→7 result move the question into parameter mechanisms and update admission. Both next steps matter, but the ordering is a real choice.')}</p>
      <div class="choice-grid">
        <div class="choice north"><span>{t('向北', 'NORTH')}</span><h3>{t('先把机制证据做深', 'Deepen the mechanism evidence first')}</h3><p>{t('收 TaskVector 因果干预，再把 GDR / DirectApply 做成完整对照。回答：OpenEVO 为什么变强，什么更新真正有用？', 'Finish TaskVector causal interventions and the GDR / DirectApply comparison. Answer: why does OpenEVO improve, and which updates actually matter?')}</p></div>
        <div class="choice south"><span>{t('向南', 'SOUTH')}</span><h3>{t('先把 SEED 匹配比较做齐', 'Complete the matched SEED comparison first')}</h3><p>{t('把训练条件尽量匹配后完成最终测试。回答：在相近资源和协议下，OpenEVO 和 SEED 到底差多少？', 'Match the training conditions as closely as possible and finish the final evaluation. Answer: under comparable resources and protocol, how far apart are OpenEVO and SEED?')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="decision-note"><strong>{t('想请老师和学长判断优先级：', 'Advisor decision:')}</strong><p>{t('先追“为什么有效”的机制证据，还是先追“到底差多少”的对外比较结果？', 'first deepen the evidence for why it works, or first finish the externally legible comparison of how much it differs?')}</p></div>
      <div class="engineering-strip">
        <strong>{t('我们解决的工程性问题（这里只列，不展开）', 'Engineering problems we resolved (listed only)')}</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>{t('动作接口与解析导致的无效动作', 'invalid actions caused by action-interface / parsing issues')}</li>
          <li>{t('长实验中断后的安全续跑与状态恢复', 'safe resume and state recovery after long-run interruptions')}</li>
          <li>{t('多卡任务分配与空闲 GPU 动态回填', 'multi-GPU scheduling and dynamic backfill of idle GPUs')}</li>
          <li>{t('checkpoint、证据、W&B / HF 的实验身份与归档', 'experiment identity and archival across checkpoints, evidence, W&B, and HF')}</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p class="final-source"><a href={flowHref}>{t('实验流程', 'Experiment flow')}</a> · <a href={technicalHref}>{t('技术推导与实验严谨性', 'Technical derivations and rigor')}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>

<script is:inline>
  const syncBriefingScale = () => {
